WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.767
We have mentioned

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.901
the former president

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.903
once again made history today,

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.805
becoming the very first former

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.874
president of the United States of America

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.042
to ever be arrested

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.744
and arraigned in a federal court

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:12.979
and the first to face federal charges

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:15.315
before heading into court today, Mr.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.716
Trump wrote on his social media

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.317
site, quote,

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:18.785
One of the saddest days

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.887
in the history of the country, unquote.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.789
I think that that's true,

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.324
although probably not in the way

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.558
he intended it.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:26.092
Joining me,

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:26.926
two people who know

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.095
about another sad and historic moment,

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.830
the Watergate scandal.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.165
Legendary investigative journalist

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.767
and author of Chasing History

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.902
A Kid in the NEWSROOM, Carl Bernstein.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:36.770
Also with me

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.505
is CNN contributor and former counsel

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:39.906
for the Nixon White House.

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:40.540
John Dean.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.074
Carl, first,

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.742
I just want to get your reaction

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.443
to what happened

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:44.844
today, these historic images

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:45.879
out of Miami.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.081
Donald Trump arriving at the courthouse.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.082
What went through your mind

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.417
watching it all?

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.151
That we're being

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.585
tested in this country

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.021
in a way that we never have been before.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.656
Then our political institutions

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:57.824
are being tested.

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.993
The Republican Party is being tested,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.861
that the judicial system

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:05.331
is being tested, that all of the elements

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.400
of who we are as a people

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.635
are being tested.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.104
As a result of one man's recklessness.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.373
One man's not caring about

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.507
what he does as president

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.708
of the United States

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.376
to the country,

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.111
but rather his own interests

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.146
throughout his presidency

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.347
and the recklessness

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.582
and disregard

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.018
for truth, for established procedure.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.853
And what's so stunning to me

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.388
today is to hear

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.856
from the Republican Party.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.192
And this is one of the great differences

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:32.992
with Watergate,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.260
where the Republican Party

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.762
eventually coalesced

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.963
against Richard Nixon

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.865
and said a criminal president

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.234
of the United States had to leave office.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.269
We don't see that happening now.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.873
Rather, what we see is this indictment.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:48.541
Trump several

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.577
Republicans are saying, yeah, he did it.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.745
It's evident from the indictment

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:53.413
he did it.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.714
He did those things.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.483
It's incontrovertible.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:59.052
And yet they're trying to make the issue,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.286
the judiciary,

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.988
the president of the United States,

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.990
Hunter Biden, Hillary Clinton.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.159
What about the criminal acts

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.661
that are incontrovertible?

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.598
In this document and made so clear

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.999
in that courtroom?

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:13.933
John Dean, the former

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.068
president's codefendant,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.971
while Nada is an interesting figure

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:18.805
in all of this,

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.174
he did not enter a plea today.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:24.010
He did not have an attorney from Florida.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.246
His arraignment will be later this month.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.548
What do you make of that?

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.817
Donald Trump shows up with attorneys.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:31.951
They are co-defendants.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.453
Walton on a does not have an attorney

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.789
Well, I remember when

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.657
there was another group

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.727
of coconspirators who after Watergate,

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.362
certainly went their own direction

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.130
and did not hang out together.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.598
So it's kind of surprising.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.067
I think if he had a good lawyer,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.302
he'd be telling him

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.970
that he ought to be doing his own thing

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.772
and strike his own pose.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.707
So it was a little bit confusing

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.843
that he is hanging and tidy.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.312
I guess he's still employed by Mr. Trump.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.780
He is still his valet,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.250
and he doesn't seem to appreciate that.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.752
Mr.
Trump is the one who got him

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.654
in the whole heap of trouble he's in

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.055
and he is in a heap of trouble.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.591
So it was unusual today,

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.927
a member of the saying the aphorism,

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:15.562
no man is a hero to his valet,

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:16.996
but that might not be true

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:17.964
in the case of Mr.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.066
Nader, he might actually still be quite

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.535
enamored of Mr. Trump. John?

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.304
Who do you think the obstruction case

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.673
is more clear cut against

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.274
what Nana or Donald Trump

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.744
Well, with a conspiracy,

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.546
all you have to do is show

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:37.050
that there is a mutual agreement, either

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.786
openly or by tacitly

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.554
to commit a criminal act.

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:42.689
I think there is

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.023
the evidence is pretty strong.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.391
They both agreed

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.193
to undertake these activities

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.429
and did the first step

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:49.862
In fact,

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.064
they did many steps

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.533
to implement the conspiracy.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:54.167
So I think

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.336
that charge is going to be very easy.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:57.403
It's a favorite

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.172
of the federal prosecutors

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.408
they use 80 USC three 71 regularly,

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.510
and that's the one they're charged under.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.579
So I think that

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.082
the conspiracy count is probably equal

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.985
I think the obstruction count

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.820
is certainly stronger against Mr.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:14.721
Trump.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:17.357
Karl, immediately after his arrest

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:17.757
and arraignment,

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.792
Donald Trump stopped at a Cuban-American

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.896
cafe in Miami where he was greeted

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:24.731
by supporters,

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:25.832
greeted by religious leaders.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:28.001
They had a little prayer circle for him.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.669
Then he flew to New Jersey.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.437
He's holding a fundraiser

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.273
in Bedminster this evening.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.008
Does this behavior surprise you at all?

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.342
Not in the least.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.611
There's every bit of evidence

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.680
that this event,

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.916
these indictments, plural, and others

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.084
in all likelihood

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:47.687
to come work to his advantage.

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.088
So far,

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:52.125
in terms of who Republican voters are.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:53.993
There was just some comment

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:54.961
a couple of moments ago

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.096
about when Iowa, the primary,

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.164
the caucuses,

00:04:58.164 --> 00:04:59.132
and primaries there

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.501
in New Hampshire occur.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:04.070
Everybody I've talked to Republicans

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.371
and I've talked to more Republicans

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.507
today, and I have Democrats

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.575
see that this is working to Trump's

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.711
advantage electorally.

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.113
But there are some subtle shifts.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.983
We heard Chris Sununu tonight

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:18.818
on this earlier broadcast,

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:20.720
and he makes great sense.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.523
But are fellow Republicans

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:26.359
going to go along and don't dump Trump?

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:29.662
We don't see much evidence of that.

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.698
And a really horrible thing is

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.499
what is the Republican Party

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.901
stand for today?

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.236
If this law and order party

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:40.006
is willing to go along with a president

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.874
who has broken the law

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.543
throughout his presidency,

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:46.446
who is being indicted in multiple cases

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.781
with incontrovertible evidence

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.016
of what he did?

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.051
Might he be acquitted by a jury?

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.654
Sure. But is the evidence there?

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:55.855
Has it been there

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:57.423
in terms of what he did?

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.459
Let's look at January 6th.

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:01.060
We know what he did.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.196
Republicans know what he did.

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:04.831
So the question becomes,

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:07.133
what about the rule of law

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:07.934
in this country?

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:09.602
And is one party

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:12.305
ready to scuttle the principle

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.706
of the rule of law

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.641
being paramount in our culture

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:16.976
and in our politics?

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:17.443
John Dean,

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.011
the former president, is quoted

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.246
in the indictment saying, quote,

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.781
I don't want anybody

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.249
looking through my boxes,

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.550
unquote, and also, quote,

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.518
wouldn't it be better

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:26.386
if we just told them

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.521
we don't have anything here?

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:29.055
These are comments

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:30.623
he made to his attorneys.

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:31.791
There's also apparently an audio

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:34.060
recording of him telling Mark Meadows

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.863
autobiography is that the document

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.131
he is showing them

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.999
is secret, that he could,

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:40.833
when he was president,

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.268
could he could he could declassify it.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.370
But since he's no longer president,

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.172
he had no ability to do so.

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:48.241
Do you see any parallels to

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:49.642
the Watergate tape

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:51.811
where Nixon is heard plotting

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:52.912
with his chief of staff?

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:56.349
Well, of course, almost

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:57.784
virtually every conversation

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:59.118
that Nixon had, he had over

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:00.586
a thousand conversations

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.155
that were recorded,

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:03.990
some of them as short as 5 minutes.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.092
Some of them 8 hours, one of them

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:09.595
where he's talking about Watergate.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:12.965
So the volume certainly is much vaster

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:14.300
with Nixon

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.702
but these are quite incriminating

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.271
and very powerful evidence,

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:21.073
the ones that they've got,

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:24.010
some of those the tapes are Mr.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.012
Cochran himself

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.581
giving his recollection of meetings

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:31.517
and apparently simultaneously

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.820
with the events are relatively close

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:35.621
based on notes.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.156
Those are going to be contested,

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:39.625
I'm sure, in this criminal trial.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:40.426
They'll probably try

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.594
to get those thrown out,

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:43.596
as George Conway was suggesting.

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:44.430
I think that's

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.565
one of their strategies

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.567
to get eliminate those.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:48.701
So anyway,

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.870
tapes are always very powerful

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:51.737
for juries.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.473
And there were about 12

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:54.106
of them were played

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.975
during the trial of Haldeman,

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:58.644
Erlichman, Mitchell at all,

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.546
who were Nixon's closest aides.

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:01.047
And they were

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:03.583
very persuasive to the jury Hmm.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:04.784
John Dean, Carl

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.152
Bernstein, thank you so much.

